// Patch 270, Stage 2: MOVED UP, from just after sv_saveloc.qc.
//
// QuakeC has no forward declarations, so a file can only read globals that an
// earlier file declared.  Stage 2 makes the timer, the recorder and the
// save-loc list behave differently in a lobby, which means sv_timer.qc and
// sv_saveloc.qc have to be able to read lobby_on -- and it was declared after
// them.  The alternative was a second copy of the cvar reads in each file,
// which is the shape that produced the ui_rs_armed bug this tree already ate.
//
// Safe to move because sv_lobby.qc depends on NOTHING in this project: grep it
// and every identifier it touches is either its own lobby_ prefix or an engine
// builtin/field from defs/sv_defs.qc.  It is only ever CALLED from later files
// (sv_player.qc's connect/disconnect, sv_main.qc's frame), and calls still run
// downhill.
server/sv_lobby.qc

server/sv_timer.qc
server/sv_saveloc.qc
server/sv_player.qc
server/sv_main.qc
